## [REDACTION] Prose — no hard-wrap

For any prose meant to be read as rendered output (README, docs, reports, emails, messages): a paragraph stays on a single logical line, never a manual line break in the middle of a sentence just to fit a fixed column width (a habit inherited from code/comment formatting, unsuited to Markdown or text meant to be rendered). Leave line wrapping to the renderer's/editor's automatic wrap. Only break a line manually for an actual structural boundary (end of paragraph, list item, table row).

