## [ARCHIVES] Logging validated functional studies and plans

As soon as a plan, analysis, or functional study is validated by the user for implementation, log the complete artifact in a local `.md` file under `ARCHIVES_R/{model}-analyses/` (e.g. `ARCHIVES_R/claude-analyses/`, `ARCHIVES_R/gemini-analyses/`, `ARCHIVES_R/opencode-analyses/`, `ARCHIVES_R/qwen-analyses/`). Naming: `YYYY-MM-DDTHH-MM-short-topic-name.md`.

**Strict ban on external publication**: every deliverable stays strictly local, in `.md` format, under `ARCHIVES_R/`. Never publish to a third-party Cloud/Artifact service.

## [GRAPHIFY] Knowledge graph — per-project method

The code graph (`graphify`) is **per project**, never global at Home:
- Before exploring code blindly (broad grep, exploratory reading), query the graph first if present in the project (`graphify-out/`): `graphify query "<question>"`, `graphify explain "<Symbol>"`, `graphify path "A" "B"`.
- After any change that significantly alters the code structure, regenerate via `graphify update .` (incremental, AST-only).
